gaoK(){return"Welcome to Skapers\xf8k!"},
gaoJ(){return"Skapers\xf8k is an inventory management app that lets you keep track of all your belongings in a simple and intuitive way \ud83d\udc4c. \n \n Before you start, let's get you up to speed with the basics."},
gaoM(){return"Architecture"},
gaoL(){return"Skapers\xf8k consists of two main components; the app (the thing you are using right now \ud83d\ude09) and the server. \n \n Using this app you fetch and edit data stored on the server. You can host a server yourself, or connect to an existing one."},
gaoO(){return"Organization"},
gaoN(){return"Skapers\xf8k organizes your items kind of like the folders on your computer, with some items inside other items. But in skapers\xf8k we dont have files and folders, we have \u2728the crate\u2728 \n \n Each blue box in the image represents a crate, as you can see they can contain other crates, but do not have to. Everything is a crate, which makes skapers\xf8k endlessly flexible! \ud83d\ude0a"},
gaoQ(){return"Placement codes"},
gaoP(){return'Maybe you noticed the green boxes above each crate? These are the placement codes. Each crate gets a short, unique code like "A-1-B". \n \n The code consists of the parents placement code, plus a layer-unique segment for the crate itself. Together they form a unique identifier for each crate that tells you it\'s location in the hierarchy. \n\nJust follow the code \u2728'},
